<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Casa de Contratación</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Casa de Contratación, or House of Trade, was the Spanish crown agency founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> in 1503 to regulate trade and navigation with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>. It licensed voyages, collected duties and trained pilots. Its monopoly directed American <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> through Spanish ports, generating customs revenues for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/casa-de-contratacion.jpg" alt="Casa de Contratación" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FlyingCrimsonPig · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Real_Alc%C3%A1zar_de_Sevilla,_Sevilla_(42052074324).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
